1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,400
Saturday, 4:37 a.m.

2
00:00:02,400 --> 00:00:05,233
This man has not told his family yet.

3
00:00:05,233 --> 00:00:08,067
Telling them ruins it. That's how surprises work.

4
00:00:08,067 --> 00:00:10,033
Delivery boxes: seventeen.

5
00:00:10,033 --> 00:00:13,133
He hid the receipt behind the frozen dumplings.

6
00:00:13,133 --> 00:00:14,767
All… or nothing!

7
00:00:15,267 --> 00:00:17,233
Dad, my butt is sitting on wood.

8
00:00:17,233 --> 00:00:18,567
Where… are we going?

9
00:00:18,567 --> 00:00:19,933
Uh… the mart?

10
00:00:19,933 --> 00:00:22,000
To the mart, with firewood?

11
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:24,233
This came out from behind the dumplings.

12
00:00:24,233 --> 00:00:25,533
Two point three million won.

13
00:00:25,533 --> 00:00:28,800
It's installments. Split into twelve, it's basically free.

14
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:30,767
Installments are not free.

15
00:00:30,767 --> 00:00:33,767
This weekend I want to lie down. Horizontally.

16
00:00:33,767 --> 00:00:35,267
You can lie horizontally in a tent too!

17
00:00:35,267 --> 00:00:36,133
On dirt?

18
00:00:36,133 --> 00:00:38,333
Dad, where's the bathroom at the campsite?

19
00:00:38,333 --> 00:00:40,333
Nature… is the bathroom.

20
00:00:40,333 --> 00:00:41,267
…Nature?

21
00:00:41,267 --> 00:00:44,667
In two kilometers, the route splits.

22
00:00:44,667 --> 00:00:48,233
Left: campsite. Eighty-seven kilometers.

23
00:00:48,233 --> 00:00:51,200
Right: home. Three kilometers.

24
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:51,833
Three.

25
00:00:51,833 --> 00:00:55,367
Note: sixty percent chance of rain at the campsite.

26
00:00:55,367 --> 00:00:57,633
So forty percent it won't rain!

27
00:00:57,633 --> 00:00:59,000
…So that's how you heard it.

28
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:01,933
Mr. Mo? About your site, B-7.

29
00:01:01,933 --> 00:01:04,867
After last night's rain, it's a swimming pool now.

30
00:01:04,867 --> 00:01:08,033
Come anyway. Lots of frogs, kids love it.

31
00:01:08,033 --> 00:01:09,567
Frogs?! Let's go!

32
00:01:09,567 --> 00:01:11,967
Frogs?! Let's go home!

33
00:01:11,967 --> 00:01:14,333
Decide. One kilometer.

34
00:01:14,333 --> 00:01:16,500
At times like this… leave it to fate.

35
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:18,733
Yut sticks… are camping essentials.

36
00:01:18,733 --> 00:01:19,867
You bought those too?

37
00:01:19,867 --> 00:01:23,033
Mo, we camp. Do, we go home.

38
00:01:23,033 --> 00:01:24,000
And if it's neither?

39
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,400
Then… I can never close the trunk again.

40
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:27,633
Mo… or Do!

41
00:01:27,633 --> 00:01:29,367
You throw the sticks.

42
00:01:29,367 --> 00:01:33,733
Press Mo for camping, Do for home.
